## API contract

The public client is generated from `openapi/public.json` into `packages/public-api-client`. Import its operations, schemas, and TanStack Query options through the package instead of writing parallel request or response types in this app. Do not edit `src/generated` in that package.

After changing [% if backend_language == "go" %]Huma operations or HTTP types[% else %]Utoipa operations or HTTP DTOs[% endif %], run the transactional contract command from the repository root. It stages every OpenAPI document and client before replacing committed output:

    <<[ web_run_command ]>> contract:generate

[% if backend_language == "go" %]`scripts/jig check contract`[% else %]`cargo test`[% endif %] rejects stale OpenAPI documents. `scripts/check-webapps.sh typecheck` runs `contract:check`, which regenerates every contract in a temporary directory and rejects drift without modifying the worktree. The build gate also scans public application artifacts for privileged package, contract, and binary markers.

A full `scripts/jig dev` session supplies the current backend through `JIG_DEV_API_ORIGIN`, which takes precedence over an inherited generic override. For a direct Vite start or `scripts/jig dev --app <frontend-name>` against a separately managed backend, set `API_ORIGIN`. Replace the starter with the first product feature while keeping the tested API boundary or evolving it with the backend.

## End-to-end tests

From the repository root after bootstrap has installed dependencies, install the Chromium test browser once and run the package-local Playwright suite through the generated exact-package boundary:

    scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <<[ frontend_dir ]>> test:e2e:install
    scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <<[ frontend_dir ]>> test:e2e

Playwright starts Vite and the production [% if backend_language == "go" %]Go[% else %]Rust[% endif %] API on isolated loopback ports, waits for `/health/ready`, and verifies the browser-observed API response. Use `scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <<[ frontend_dir ]>> test:e2e:ui` while authoring tests. Failure traces, screenshots, and the HTML report are written to ignored directories.

The defaults avoid the development database and are unique to this package. [% if backend_language == "rust" %]SQLite scaffolds reset the ignored `.agent/tmp/<<[ e2e_database_name ]>>.sqlite` and its `-shm`, `-wal`, and `-journal` sidecars before each run; [% endif %]Postgres scaffolds use `postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/<<[ e2e_database_name ]>>` and require a reachable disposable Postgres server. Set `E2E_DATABASE_URL` to use a different disposable database, `E2E_API_PORT` or `E2E_WEB_PORT` when the default ports are occupied (the API and web ports must differ), `E2E_SERVER_TIMEOUT_MS` for a slow cold [% if backend_language == "go" %]Go compilation[% else %]Rust build[% endif %], `E2E_GLOBAL_TIMEOUT_MS` to override the CI suite budget, or `E2E_BASE_URL` to test an already-running environment without starting local servers. The default CI suite budget includes both sequential local-server startup timeouts plus five minutes of test headroom, with a ten-minute minimum; the generated GitHub Actions job allows 30 minutes so dependency setup and installation remain outside that Playwright budget. PostgreSQL E2E uses its own Ubuntu runner because GitHub service containers require Linux; the scaffold workflow is project-owned after init if a self-hosted Linux label is preferred.
